        <body>
            <div xml:id="d935">

                <pb facs="0955" n="843" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg843"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 892.001/4.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Siamese Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-10-25"><hi rendition="#italic">October 25,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have the honor to acknowledge with deep regret the receipt of your telegram of
                    yesterday’s date conveying the sad intelligence of the death of His Majesty King
                    Chulalongkorn on October 23.</p>
                <p>The President, to whom the information was duly conveyed, has cabled his
                    condolence to King Maha Vajiravudh and I take this occasion to express to you
                    the deep sympathy of the Government and people of the United States and my own
                    sincere condolence in the national loss sustained by your country.</p>
                <p>I would be pleased if you informed the department as to the date on which the
                    funeral services will take place.</p>
                <closer>(For <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr.
                            Knox.</hi></signed>)<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A.
                            Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
